From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Cheng <dcheng@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:13:11 -0800
Subject: Use owned iterators in XML parser xml_ffi

`AttributesIterator` and `NamespacesIterator` wrap Rust iterators for
C++ code to consume. They stored borrowed iterators internally, so the
Rust structs required an explicit lifetime annotation. In turn, this
meant that the FFI helpers on the Rust side of the cxx bridge needed to
be marked unsafe, since the C++ compiler cannot enforce Rust's lifetime
annotations.

As of https://crrev.com/c/8521957, the Rust side makes a clone of the
declared namespaces to avoid holding a borrow on shared state when
calling into C++, so `NamespacesIterator` can just consume the clone and
completely avoid lifetime annotations. This CL takes it one step further
by preprocessing the strings on the Rust side to avoid intermediate
string constructions in C++ and updates the FFI plumbing to pass Rust
`str`s in the same style as the pre-existing `AttributeView`.

`AttributesIterator` can also consume its input, so similarly update it
to hold a consuming iterator and drop the lifetime annotations.

Bug: 569659189
Change-Id: I9a9077939ac45fe40d1cff0b8f7e07b26a40cb1e
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8667670
Reviewed-by: Joey Arhar <jarhar@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Daniel Cheng <dcheng@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1735370}

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y): this branch's xml_ffi.rs computes the
newly declared namespaces itself (new_namespaces()/namespace_stack) and used to
filter the synthesized xml/xmlns entries in namespaces_next(). The owned
NamespacesIterator is therefore built from that computed Namespace instead of
declared_namespaces(): the same xml/xmlns filter is applied while collecting,
and the (q_name, uri) pairs are preprocessed exactly as upstream (empty prefix
-> empty q_name, else "xmlns:" + prefix) so the C++ NamespaceView side applies
verbatim. AttributesIterator, attributes_next, namespaces_next, the cxx bridge
declarations and the C++ changes apply as upstream.

